title: World War One
subject: History
level: GCSE
emoji: 🪖
description: Causes, key battles, trench warfare and the end of the war.
---
When did World War One begin and end? :: 28 July 1914 – 11 November 1918.
Which event sparked WW1? :: The assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand in Sarajevo, 28 June 1914.
What does MAIN stand for (long-term causes)? :: Militarism, Alliances, Imperialism, Nationalism.
Which countries made up the Triple Entente? :: Britain, France and Russia.
Which countries made up the Triple Alliance? :: Germany, Austria-Hungary and Italy.
What was the Schlieffen Plan? :: Germany's plan to defeat France quickly through Belgium, then turn on Russia.
Why did Britain enter the war in August 1914? :: Germany invaded neutral Belgium, whose neutrality Britain had guaranteed.
What was 'no man's land'? :: The dangerous area between opposing trenches.
What was the first major battle of 1914 that stopped Germany's advance? :: The First Battle of the Marne.
Which battle began on 1 July 1916 and saw 57,000 British casualties on day one? :: The Battle of the Somme.
Which 1916 battle was the longest of the war, between France and Germany? :: Verdun.
Which 1917 battle was fought in deep mud in Belgium? :: Passchendaele (Third Battle of Ypres).
What new weapon did Britain introduce at the Somme? :: The tank.
What was 'shell shock'? :: A psychological condition caused by prolonged exposure to combat.
What was the Gallipoli campaign? :: A failed Allied attempt in 1915 to take the Dardanelles from the Ottoman Empire.
Why did Germany's unrestricted submarine warfare matter? :: It brought the USA into the war in April 1917.
What caused Russia to leave the war? :: The 1917 revolutions; Russia signed the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk in March 1918.
When was the Armistice signed? :: 11 November 1918 at 11 a.m.
What was the Treaty of Versailles? :: The 1919 peace treaty that blamed Germany for the war and imposed reparations.
What was the League of Nations? :: An international organisation set up in 1920 to keep peace.
What was conscription? :: Compulsory enrolment in the armed forces – introduced in Britain in 1916.
